WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.547
Three Claude models got the same brief.

00:00:02.547 --> 00:00:06.142
A two-storey beach house, every plank written in Python, that you can

00:00:06.142 --> 00:00:07.640
walk through in a browser.

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.774
These are the three files, in this site's own viewer.

00:00:10.774 --> 00:00:12.426
One was done in forty-two minutes.

00:00:12.426 --> 00:00:13.528
Which would you keep?

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:16.596
Hi, I'm Dormer!

00:00:16.596 --> 00:00:19.552
Let's walk through all three, and see what each one cost.

00:00:24.683 --> 00:00:26.826
The loop is the same for all three.

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:29.238
A Python script builds the whole scene from nothing.

00:00:29.638 --> 00:00:34.180
Blender's Cycles bakes the light into textures, so the browser never computes a shadow.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:38.533
Geometry and atlases go into one file of about five megabytes.

00:00:38.933 --> 00:00:41.497
Headless Chromium screenshots it in the site's viewer.

00:00:41.897 --> 00:00:45.054
And a brand new subagent, one that has seen nothing else,

00:00:45.054 --> 00:00:46.202
answers yes or no.

00:00:46.202 --> 00:00:47.063
Then go again.

00:00:48.825 --> 00:00:49.862
Opus went first.

00:00:49.862 --> 00:00:51.937
Seven passes, four critics, four noes.

00:00:51.937 --> 00:00:53.320
The last one said:

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:54.904
No, but it is close.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:58.358
It built the best-dressed site of the three.

00:00:58.358 --> 00:01:01.835
A dune fence, a boardwalk to a fire pit, an outdoor shower.

00:01:02.215 --> 00:01:04.414
And it wrote the viewer the other two were tested in.

00:01:05.908 --> 00:01:07.882
Fable never asked Cycles for colour.

00:01:07.882 --> 00:01:12.158
It baked only the light, and painted the boards and shingles in afterwards.

00:01:12.538 --> 00:01:15.164
Five critics: no, no, no, yes, yes.

00:01:15.164 --> 00:01:17.415
About ninety-three minutes, across three machines.

00:01:17.795 --> 00:01:20.240
Out on the balcony you can see what that bought.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.195
The rail shadows are part of the texture.

00:01:24.533 --> 00:01:28.884
Sonnet built its geometry in pure Python, before Blender ever saw it.

00:01:28.884 --> 00:01:32.148
About four thousand one hundred and sixty flat faces.

00:01:32.528 --> 00:01:35.528
Its third critic said yes, after about forty-two minutes.

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:37.528
The fastest yes on the page.

00:01:37.908 --> 00:01:39.372
The architecture is crisp.

00:01:39.372 --> 00:01:41.201
The furniture is plain boxes.

00:01:42.867 --> 00:01:44.693
Put the three loops on one clock.

00:01:44.693 --> 00:01:46.257
Each stamp is a critic's verdict.

00:01:46.677 --> 00:01:48.058
Sonnet: no, no, yes.

00:01:50.277 --> 00:01:52.367
Opus: four noes, the last one close.

00:01:54.077 --> 00:01:57.370
Fable: three noes, then two yeses, at about twice the time.

00:01:58.477 --> 00:01:59.827
So which house is best?

00:01:59.827 --> 00:02:00.907
A critic can't say.

00:02:00.907 --> 00:02:02.526
It only answers: is this done?

00:02:04.367 --> 00:02:06.637
So the article ran a blind test.

00:02:06.637 --> 00:02:10.528
Eleven matched views of all three houses, shown to three fresh judges

00:02:10.528 --> 00:02:11.825
with the names removed.

00:02:12.205 --> 00:02:15.715
Reveal the names, and every judge's ranking is there, view by view.

00:02:17.433 --> 00:02:18.757
Thirty-three judgements in all.

00:02:20.433 --> 00:02:22.332
Fable took seventeen first places.

00:02:22.332 --> 00:02:23.471
Opus took sixteen.

00:02:23.471 --> 00:02:26.130
Sonnet, with the fastest yes, took none.

00:02:27.617 --> 00:02:29.204
The split is not random.

00:02:29.204 --> 00:02:31.425
From the air, Opus won every judgement.

00:02:31.425 --> 00:02:33.011
Its site tells the story.

00:02:33.391 --> 00:02:36.977
At eye level, where a visitor actually stands, Fable's baked light won

00:02:36.977 --> 00:02:39.368
the deck and the balcony with every judge.

00:02:40.475 --> 00:02:42.669
A critic's yes means nothing is visibly broken.

00:02:42.669 --> 00:02:44.862
It does not mean the house is good.

00:02:44.862 --> 00:02:46.508
Rounds are what you pay for.

00:02:48.275 --> 00:02:50.722
Sonnet got the fastest yes and came last.

00:02:50.722 --> 00:02:53.781
Fable won narrowly, and Opus is best from the air.

00:02:53.781 --> 00:02:55.311
Go and walk them yourself.

00:02:55.311 --> 00:02:56.229
Thanks for watching!

00:02:56.649 --> 00:02:58.750
Every source is in the full article.

00:02:58.750 --> 00:02:59.350
I'm Dormer.

00:02:59.350 --> 00:02:59.650
Bye!
